 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions use [web process memory](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-web-process-memory.md).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A restart or deploy clears sessions; members must log in again.
+- Sessions are not shared across processes or servers. Run one web process or configure sticky routing to keep a
+  member's requests on the process that holds their session; sticky routing does not preserve sessions on restart.
+- Expired sessions are not evicted from the dict. Restarting the process reclaims the memory and logs members out.
 
 ## Shaped by
 
